# ── Operational alerting → Slack (services/alertService.js) ───────────
# ONE secret, and it lives in Render env only, deliberately absent here:
#   SLACK_BOT_TOKEN
#
# The CHANNELS are not secret — a channel id or #name discloses nothing and
# is useless without the token — so they live here with every other
# non-secret public id, and changing where alerts go is a committed,
# reviewable diff instead of an untracked dashboard edit. Real env still
# wins over this file (index.js loads env first, dotenv never overrides an
# already-set var), so a single service can still be pointed elsewhere from
# the Render dashboard without a deploy.
#
# Alerts stay silently disabled until SLACK_BOT_TOKEN is set, so shipping
# these channel values changes nothing on its own.
SLACK_ALERT_CHANNEL=C0BMMDA3MFE
# Separate channel for `fatal` only; falls back to the main one if blank.
SLACK_ALERT_CHANNEL_FATAL=C0BM2BG6M71
# Per-run live feed (services/runFeedService.js). One parent message per
# CampaignRun (chat.update'd on a throttle = the live status screen), with
# the full chronological event log as threaded replies batched on a short
# interval. Completely inert without SLACK_BOT_TOKEN. Poll ticks are
# filtered from the thread; they only refresh the parent's "now:" line.
SLACK_ALERT_CHANNEL_STATUS=C0BMMD5AN84
# RUN_FEED_ENABLED — master switch. Default ON when the channel is set;
#   set false to mute the feed without unsetting the channel.
# RUN_FEED_PARENT_THROTTLE_MS — min ms between chat.update of the parent
#   (live counts / stages / elapsed). Final finish always flushes.
# RUN_FEED_THREAD_FLUSH_MS — detached interval that drains the ring buffer
#   into threaded posts. All Slack I/O happens here, never on a render path.
# RUN_FEED_RING_SIZE — fixed per-run event buffer. When full, DROP OLDEST
#   and count the drops; the next post reports "(N events dropped)".
RUN_FEED_ENABLED=true
RUN_FEED_PARENT_THROTTLE_MS=10000
RUN_FEED_THREAD_FLUSH_MS=2000
RUN_FEED_RING_SIZE=200
#
# ALERT_MIN_LEVEL — info | warn | error | fatal. 'warn' mutes the
#   per-boot "started" line; set 'info' to watch instance restarts live
#   (Render autoscaling replaces the web instance on its own, and each
#   replacement kills any in-flight render loop).
# ALERT_DEDUPE_WINDOW_MIN — a given alert key sends at most once per
#   window; repeats are counted and folded into the next delivery.
# ALERT_RATE_LIMIT_MAX — hard ceiling on messages per minute.
# ALERT_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MIN — health-sweep cadence in the worker.
# ALERT_RENDERING_STALE_MIN — must stay BELOW REAP_STALE_MIN (15) so a
#   wedged render is reported before the reaper rewrites the evidence.
# ALERT_RUN_STALE_MIN — a 20-ad video batch at VEO_CONCURRENCY=4 is far
#   shorter than the old ~25-35min serial (VEO=1) path; 45m still clears it.
# ALERT_HOURLY_SPEND_USD — trailing-hour CostLog total that trips a
#   warning. Video dominates, but the old justification here was WRONG and
#   this threshold was tuned against it: it claimed a 4:5 canvas cannot run
#   on Omni and falls back to Grok at $0.50/s (~$4.00 for an 8s clip).
#   It does not. `omniFamilyNativeFor()` (atlasVideoService.js:508-522) ends
#   `return r < 1 ? '9:16' : '16:9'`, so 4:5 routes to Omni 9:16 and 1:1 does
#   too unless SQUARE_VIA_OMNI_CROP=false; the compositor then crops
#   face-anchored. Grok is only the square opt-out and explicitly-selected
#   non-Omni models. Real Omni cost is `(4k ? $1 : $0.2) + duration x $0.1`
#   = **$1.00 for an 8s 1080p clip**, roughly 4x LOWER than the old comment.
#   So this ceiling is ~4x too high to catch what it was meant to catch —
#   re-tune it against measured CostLog rather than the stale figure.
ALERTS_ENABLED=true
ALERT_MIN_LEVEL=warn
ALERT_DEDUPE_WINDOW_MIN=15
ALERT_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=20
ALERT_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MIN=5
ALERT_RENDERING_STALE_MIN=12
ALERT_RUN_STALE_MIN=45
ALERT_DETECT_BACKLOG_COUNT=25
ALERT_DETECT_BACKLOG_MIN=20
ALERT_HOURLY_SPEND_USD=25

# Static direct-overlay plate generation. MEASURED 2026-07-31: a real
# openai/gpt-image-2/edit call with this service's exact payload (1 reference,
# 1024x1024, quality medium) took 69.7s. The former 60s bound sat below that
# floor and failed most renders intermittently, while still being billed —
# Atlas charges on submit. 600s is deliberately generous: the poller now reads
# Atlas's error envelope, so a long ceiling is only spent on requests that are
# genuinely still processing. Keep it BELOW REAP_STALE_MIN (default 15m/900s),
# past which a render can be reclaimed and re-billed. Re-measure before lowering.
AI_DIRECT_IMAGE_TIMEOUT_MS=600000

# Post-render vision QC on finished static ads (services/adVisionQcService.js).
# Compares the ORIGINAL product photo against the FINISHED render; on fail it
# regenerates exactly ONCE, then flags and stops. Each regen is a billable image
# submit and the vision call is a billable LLM call, so this is a spend decision
# as much as a quality one.
#
# DEFAULT false — ship dark. Two things must be true before flipping it: the
# 'ad-vision-qc' model role must be confirmed ROUTABLE live (a catalog listing is
# not a router guarantee — see atlasModelMap's gpt-5-nano note), and the per-ad
# cost must be accepted. Set on BOTH Render services to enable.
AD_VISION_QC_ENABLED=false
# Optional model override. Otherwise role 'ad-vision-qc' resolves via
# atlasModelMap to google/gemini-2.5-pro — NOT flash: flash was probed live
# against this exact defect and broke the requested JSON shape (returned
# competitor_marks as a bare bool and hoisted findings), which either ships a bad
# ad or burns the one regeneration for nothing.
# AD_VISION_QC_MODEL=

# ── Titling (Remotion) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# When true (default), the RENDER path ignores persisted titleStyleSpec
# override documents on ad/product/category/brand. Stale brand specs were
# permanently shadowing the canonical no-scrim cinema standard
# (remotion/presets/canonical.json). Named curated presets
# (brand.titleStylePreset → remotion/presets/<name>.json) still apply;
# canonical remains the floor. Title Studio authoring/preview passes
# honourPersistedOverrides so operators can still see/edit stored docs.
# Flip to false to restore the old override cascade without a deploy.
# Stored fields are NOT deleted — this is a read-path change only.
TITLE_SPEC_IGNORE_PERSISTED=true

# Map face/subject vision boxes onto plateHints band `avoid` flags so
# resolveGroupAnchor shifts titles off faces. Reuses Ad.basePlate detection
# when the crop path already paid for it; otherwise detects once (~$0.02,
# ledgered) and caches. false → pre-keep-out behaviour (luma-only bands,
# avoid always false in basic mode).
TITLE_FACE_KEEPOUT=true

# ── Quote tiering (services/layoutInputService.js) ───────────────────
# Brand-tier review quotes may win as a LAST-RESORT fallback on product-scoped ads (below product/category/comment tiers, never above them); set false to restore withholding brand quotes from product ads entirely.
QUOTE_BRAND_TIER_FALLBACK=true
